  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 204 PM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\n(Friday - Saturday Night)\n\nSlightly below normal temperatures are expected heading into the \nweekend behind Thursday's cold front. High temperatures both Friday \nand Saturday are expected to be mainly in the low to mid 50s and the \ncoldest so far this Fall season. A surface high is forecast to move \nsouth out of the Upper Midwest on Friday, with surface ridging \nacross our region into the weekend. The combination of a clear sky \nand light/variable winds should allow for temperatures to drop into \nthe 30s both Friday and Saturday nights. Favored valley terrain \nlikely will see their first freeze of the season, but most areas \nprobably will stay just above the freezing mark. The air mass coming \nin is not anomalous by any means (850-hPa T anomalies of 2-4C), but \nit is so late in the year that it is not that difficult to get near-\nfreezing lows behind any cold front. \n\n\n(Sunday - Next Wednesday)\n\nEnsemble guidance is in very good agreement in a dry pattern late \nthis weekend into early next week along with moderating \ntemperatures. Lows in the 40s and highs in the 60s are forecast \nthrough the period. Confidence is pretty high in these temperatures \nfor a days 3-7 forecast given very little spread in the longwave \npattern across the CONUS in the LREF. The 13Z NBM also shows this \nwell, with only a ~3-5F degree difference between the 25th and 75th \npercentiles across the region for both highs and lows.",
